WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.780
In this video, you see how Kasm Workspaces runs on SUSE Virtualization virtual machines, then log in and stream a terminal, a Windows desktop and a browser.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:18.380
Kasm is already installed on this cluster. On the Virtual Machines page, filter for kasm to see the virtual machines it uses.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:26.920
The control plane is one Ubuntu virtual machine named kasm. It runs the Kasm database, API, manager and proxy.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:37.080
The kasm-dynamic-agent virtual machines in the kasm-autoscale namespace were not created by hand. Kasm creates and deletes them through its Harvester provider.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:43.130
To see how the control plane was installed, open the Advanced Options of the kasm virtual machine.

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:51.710
Its cloud-init user data downloads Kasm 1.19 and runs the single-server installer. The passwords on the installer line are blurred.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:59.800
New agents are cloned from images in the kasm-autoscale namespace, like this Linux agent image with the workspaces already pulled.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.670
Now open the Kasm portal and log in as the demo user.

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:07.530
The password is typed into the masked field, then you select Login.

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:16.230
The dashboard lists the workspaces this user may start: browsers, Linux desktops, a terminal and Windows Server.

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:20.080
Select the Terminal workspace to open its launch dialog.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:28.210
Then select Launch Session. Kasm starts a container on a Linux agent virtual machine.

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:35.960
The terminal streams into the browser tab. Check the kernel, the CPUs and the memory that the session sees.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:39.960
When you are done, open the Kasm control panel on the left edge,

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:44.350
select Delete Session, and confirm that you want to delete it.

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:51.490
Next, select the Windows Server 2025 workspace and launch it.

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:58.980
Kasm hands you a ready Windows virtual machine and connects to it over RDP.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:03.560
The Windows desktop runs in the same browser tab, with no client to install.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:07.820
End it the same way, from the control panel with Delete Session.

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:14.960
Kasm deletes this Windows virtual machine and prepares a fresh one for the next user.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:19.680
Next, select the Chrome workspace and launch an isolated browser.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:28.970
Chrome runs in a container on the Linux agent. Select the Web Store shortcut on the new tab page.

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:36.970
The page loads inside the session, so nothing from the website runs on your own computer.

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:41.770
Delete this session too when you finish, so its resources go back to the pool.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:55.851
Kasm streams each workspace from virtual machines on the cluster, and adds or removes agent virtual machines as demand changes.
